{"type":"message","id":"47384de4","parentId":"ab27c759","timestamp":"2026-05-19T04:04:27.718Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which is good. But POST /send returns error 1101. The error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers means \"Worker threw exception\" - so the /send endpoint is throwing an exception.\n\nLet me check if maybe the message format needs different fields, or if there's a different issue. Let me try with just the required fields.\n\nActually, looking at the history responses, messages have fields like: id, content, threadId, type, timestamp, echoAsset, replyTo. Maybe the send endpoint requires different fields too.\n\nLet me try with minimal fields.\n\nWait, the error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error that happens when the Worker throws an unhandled exception. \n\nThe send endpoint is crashing, which points to a server-side bug rather than a client issue. Let me test with a simpler message to confirm this isn't a content formatting problem.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-492d6484-5899-4b58-99f4-c3aed01b96f5","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Test with simplest possible message\ncurl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":219,"output":294,"cacheRead":20240,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20753,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779163449017,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d003f1af-9d05-40b8-98b4-c21ac734334c"}}
